    "n8_poolmap_cannot_distribute": {
      "finding": "multiprocessing.Pool interception cannot execute a user-defined function on a remote worker. _ClusterPool ships the function as a pickled reference; the pool worker runs warm_worker.py from a temp directory with neither the job's workspace on sys.path nor the user's module importable, so unpickling raises AttributeError (__main__ kernel) or ModuleNotFoundError (adjacent module). Every chunk 500s and the shim falls back to local, so results stay correct and no speedup is obtained.",
